        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set (or clear) a model&apos;s registration. Setting None removes the entry so the manifest only holds models the project actually selects. Does not persist; callers invoke TryUpdateDefaultConfigFile() to write DefaultGame.ini. Returns true when this call actually changed the manifest, so a caller knows whether to write DefaultGame.ini.</para>
<para>Reported from here rather than compared by the caller, and that is the point. Callers used to decide for themselves — the Model Manager&apos;s catalog refresh skipped the whole call whenever cached <emphasis>languages</emphasis> matched the server, which meant a stale cached <emphasis>engine</emphasis> was never corrected. Every manifest written before the engine field existed therefore kept the enum default and silently pre-warmed nothing. Only this method knows what it caches, so only this method can say whether a write mattered; adding a field later cannot reintroduce the same bug. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
